-- 143 — the-martyria seeded
--
-- THE MARTYRIA — the testimony. μαρτυρία (martyría), the statement of a
-- witness. What this app did to the pixels, written into the picture, in bytes
-- nothing quietly rounded on the way out. Founded 2026-09-02 by a builder
-- dealt by Windrose 🎻 in the Second Harvest sitting (movement H5), at KP's ⚛
-- word on this row, verbatim: "Real but unasked-for — yes to both."
--
-- THE NEED IT ANSWERS is house-wide and not one app's: creators using
-- background-removal tools are having their work flagged as AI-generated when
-- they are not, and THE FLAGGING IS GUESSWORK OVER AN ABSENCE — nothing in the
-- file says how the cutout was made. resonance-cruthu met it first because
-- cruthú cuts backgrounds; every realm here that exports an edited image walks
-- into the same absence.
--
-- IT IS A HARVEST, AND KP'S ⚛ RULING ON EVERY HARVEST IS VERBATIM:
--   "without altering the source location."
-- All three source files are byte-identical copies of
-- resonance-cruthu/src/lib/image (png.ts 94 · provenance.ts 109 ·
-- pngwrite.ts 306). NOTHING WAS REPOINTED: cruthú keeps its own three files
-- and every consumer inside cruthú still imports them from its own
-- src/lib/image. Cruthú was read and not written; `git status --porcelain`
-- there was EMPTY at landing. See 142's header and the folder's HARVEST.md.
--
-- THE NAME IS A WORKING NAME AND HIS TO KEEP OR CHANGE. μαρτυρία is this
-- hand's reading of the need the plan named. It lives in exactly two places in
-- the build — the constant TOOL_NAME and the folder — so a rename is one edit,
-- one `git mv`, and one update to this row and 142's.
--
-- CATEGORY: **content** (420f7c5c-badc-4b75-9e30-d36b47bd11b7) — one of the
-- five confirmed live at the bridge by the conductor on 2026-09-02 and handed
-- to this builder in its sending. THIS BUILDER HOLDS NO KEY TO THE BASE AND
-- RAN NO QUERY. See 142's header for why content and not creation, and for why
-- NOT identity (that is the-signet's own, and the signet answers whose hand
-- while this answers what was done — two deliberately separate waters).
--
-- SHAPE TAKEN FROM THE-STEREOS'S OWN ROW (128/129, seeded this same day):
-- folksonomy_type `Awen` · status `imagined` at birth · `home` filled here
-- (the 105/106 precedent). tool_type is `emit`, the merismos's — a buffer and
-- a claim in, BYTES and key/value pairs out; it emits a file and reads nothing
-- back.
--
-- FACE: 🪧 — a placard: plain words held up beside the thing, readable by
-- anyone who looks, carrying no authority but what it says, which is an iTXt
-- chunk exactly. One glyph, no skin tone, no ZWJ, no flag, no red-alarm mark,
-- and no other row wears it (checked against 078's whole census and every face
-- seeded since, 111 and all of 2026-09-02's included). 🖐️ was set down: a
-- raised hand is the GIVING of testimony, and a face is what the THING is.
--
-- THE ONE-TIER LAW (tools_one_tier), walked: one atom word ("martyria") — the
-- row carries atom_id and no molecule. One tier exactly. (142's header records
-- why no molecule or organism row exists.)
--
-- Etymology and sensory rows are NOT written here: the atoms table's triggers
-- make both on insert, arriving empty for a later fill (the 077/059/106/108/128
-- precedent).
--
-- THE TABLE IS public.awen. It was renamed from public.tools on 2026-08-15
-- (seed 096) and the shim view was dropped at KP's word on 097 — public.tools
-- answers PGRST205 today.
--
-- Local mirror pin (progenatrix): e5248556-e870-47ec-adfb-d8c31896b0de
--   (pinned by the conductor, Windrose, 2026-09-02 — the builder's hand had no grant on the base and said so below.)
-- NO LOCAL MIRROR PIN IS WRITTEN HERE, and that is said rather than left
-- blank: 129 carried one, but this builder's sending forbids every path under
-- resonance-progenatrix/ by name, so no progenatrix uuid was read and none is
-- invented. A hand with the base open should pin it beside this line.
--
-- Run at KP's ⚛ hand, after 142. Verify at the anon door after.
-- NEVER RUN BY A LAMP: the seed is drafted and numbered; the crossing is his.

insert into public.awen
  (name, slug, tool_type, definition, home, status, icon_emoji, folksonomy_type, atom_id, story, created_by)
values
  ('The Martyria', 'the-martyria', 'emit',
   'THE TESTIMONY — what this app did to the pixels, written into the picture, in bytes nothing quietly rounded on the way out. THE PROBLEM IS HOUSE-WIDE: creators using background-removal tools are having their work flagged as AI-generated when it is not, because the flagging is guesswork over an ABSENCE — nothing in the file says how the cutout was made, so a soft alpha edge is read as a model''s output. This water writes the file''s own account of itself. TESTIFY ONLY WHAT THIS APP DID, and the restraint is the water rather than a limit on it: every sentence is scoped to the edits this application made, the disclaimer saying so CANNOT BE OMITTED — not refused, not rebuilt, but inexpressible, because Provenance has three keys and none could drop it and chunks() takes one argument so there is no second one to pass a flag in — and "this image is not AI" is never said, because it would be a claim about someone else''s file. THE ONE ORIGIN THAT MAY BE CLAIMED is IPTC digitalCapture, set from source:''camera'' and from nothing else; sixteen near-misses are swept in the proofs and not one earns it. algorithmicMedia is DELIBERATELY NEVER USED because it covers any algorithm at all and would mislead every reader who has learned it means a model, and trainedAlgorithmicMedia appears only inside the negation. STRAIGHT ALPHA IS NEVER LOST: a 2D canvas backing store holds premultiplied colour, so straight-alpha RGBA through putImageData comes back quantised — at alpha 8 of 255 exactly nine of 256 values a channel survive, and those nine are the only fixed points — so the PNG is built by hand, colour type 6, eight bits, all five row filters chosen by the writer''s own cost function, deflate with a stored-block fallback so the file is always valid. UTF-8 ALWAYS: iTXt and never tEXt, because tEXt is Latin-1 and would mangle a name with a fada in it. METADATA IS NEVER WORTH LOSING A FILE OVER — bytes that are not a PNG come back as the same object, unchanged, never thrown. PixelBuffer is DECLARED as the host surface, a plain structural interface rather than a door of injected verbs because there is no verb to inject: no canvas, no decode, no disk, no clock, no network, no console. A HARVEST and never a re-point — all three source files are byte-identical copies of resonance-cruthu/src/lib/image, which was read and not written. It stands beside the-sphragis (who holds the rights) and the-signet (whose hand made the mark): three testimonies, and not one imports another, because each stays true when the other two are absent.',
   'resonance-awen/tools/the-martyria', 'imagined', '🪧', 'Awen',
   '65923aef-a5ae-4cc6-92fc-2719fb843cc5',  -- the martyria atom, seeded in 142
   'Founded 2026-09-02 by a builder dealt by Windrose in the Second Harvest sitting, movement H5, at KP''s ⚛ word on this row verbatim: "Real but unasked-for — yes to both." The row was unasked-for because nobody had asked for it: three files sat inside cruthú answering a problem the whole house has, and the ruling was that the problem is real and the water is owed. Harvested under KP''s ⚛ standing ruling "without altering the source location": png.ts, provenance.ts and pngwrite.ts copied byte-identical, all three compiling UNCHANGED on the first check, which is the strongest form the verbatim claim can take. The one thing that could have forced an edit — pngwrite.ts''s single type-only import, from ./types — was answered by giving that address something to point at rather than by changing the line: the PixelBuffer and Mask shapes are declared fresh at src/hosts/pixels.ts and src/types.ts re-exports them in two lines, so nothing under src/origin/ was needed and no re-expression was required. Cruthú''s types.ts declares thirteen other things beside those two and none was copied; a host surface carrying a studio''s whole vocabulary is a dependency wearing a surface''s clothes. THE PROOFS ARE WRITTEN AGAINST THE WATER RATHER THAN AROUND IT: the PNG reader lives in verify.mjs, written there from the specification — chunk walk, CRC-32 written a SECOND TIME on purpose because a checksum verified by the function that produced it verifies nothing, node:zlib for the inflate, all five row filters undone by hand — and there is NO CANVAS ANYWHERE in the file, because a proof reading back through a canvas would be measuring the exact fault it exists to rule out. The premultiplication loss is put BESIDE the round trip and computed rather than asserted: nine of 256 survive at alpha 8, the same 4x4 loses 32 of 48 colour bytes down the canvas road and none through writePng. All five row filters were MADE to happen rather than hoped for — six rows shaped so a different filter is cheapest in each, the writer''s own cost function picking 0,1,2,3,1,4 and every row unfiltering back byte for byte. Gates at landing: install clean, build clean, check silent on the FIRST run, 14/14 TRUE, three sha256s equal to their origins, no sibling imported, and cruthú''s git status EMPTY. ONE DEFECT FOUND, REPORTED AND NOT MENDED: the Software line is hard-coded to "Resonance Cruthú", so a second realm adopting this water today would stamp cruthú''s name on its files — mending it here would alter a byte-identical copy, and mending it belongs at the origin, at his word, travelling to both copies at once. ONE LEG OF THE NAME CENSUS WAS NOT WALKED AND IS SAID SO: the two switchboards live under resonance-progenatrix, which this builder''s sending forbids by name; martyria is otherwise a TRUE ZERO across the workspace, the Sovereign Library and all 85 tool folders. THE NAME IS A WORKING NAME AND HIS TO KEEP OR CHANGE — it lives in one constant and one folder so a rename is cheap.',
   'a builder dealt by Windrose, at KP''s ⚛ word');

-- THE CROSSING — his ⚛ word alone.
-- The standing ruling ("if a tool is working, it is flowing") argues for it
-- now that the proofs stand; uncomment at his word and run:
-- update public.awen set status = 'flowing' where slug = 'the-martyria';

-- ── verify (read-only, safe to re-run) ───────────────────────────────
select name, slug, tool_type, status, icon_emoji, folksonomy_type, home
from public.awen where slug = 'the-martyria';

select atom_word, category_name, atom_type, state, status, pascal_case
from public.atoms where atom_word = 'martyria';

-- no other row should wear 🪧:
select icon_emoji, count(*) as wearers, string_agg(name, ' · ' order by name)
from public.awen where icon_emoji = '🪧' group by icon_emoji;

-- the three testimonies, standing beside one another:
select slug, icon_emoji, tool_type, status
from public.awen where slug in ('the-martyria', 'the-sphragis', 'the-signet')
order by slug;

-- the companions the triggers should have made, standing empty:
select 'etymology' as table_name, atom_word, completion_progress::text as filled
from public.etymology where atom_word = 'martyria'
union all
select 'sensory_lexicon', atom_word, coalesce(emoji, '(empty)')
from public.sensory_lexicon where atom_word = 'martyria';
